WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.837
Here's what you'll be able to
do by the end of this module,

2
00:00:02.837 --> 00:00:05.387
which takes about forty-five
minutes with the lab.

3
00:00:05.387 --> 00:00:09.929
You'll name the four Active Directory
group patterns in the data platform book,

4
00:00:09.929 --> 00:00:14.238
Data Platform: SQL Server Identity,
and the Entra replacement for each.

5
00:00:14.238 --> 00:00:17.966
You'll explain why a dynamic rule
reads an H R maintained code,

6
00:00:17.966 --> 00:00:20.650
and excludes disabled accounts and guests.

7
00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:23.061
You'll run the kit's
group map over fixtures,

8
00:00:23.061 --> 00:00:27.262
and read its flags for nesting and for
a privileged role on a dynamic group.

9
00:00:27.262 --> 00:00:31.737
And you'll say which check enforces one
group, one role, and why the map doesn't.

10
00:00:31.737 --> 00:00:33.658
Before you start, finish Module 4:

11
00:00:33.658 --> 00:00:37.426
its login plan is where the
one-group-one-role warning comes from.

12
00:00:37.426 --> 00:00:39.140
Lab 1 needs no tenant.
